# taxcrawler-dm — Cursor Rules

## Before any task

Read @docs/process/llm-continuity.md for current state and next steps.
Read @docs/specification/system-modules.md for module responsibilities.
Read @docs/process/spec-rules.md for rules that must never be violated.

## Segment hierarchy

cli/ api/ ui/ -> services/ -> core/
Never skip a layer. core/ has no knowledge of any other segment.

## Code conventions

- Code in English
- Comments and docstrings in Spanish (ASCII only, no accents or tildes)
- sys.exit() only in cli/main.py
- Every user-visible action produces a log entry
- Passwords never stored in any file

## libs/ path resolution

\_libs = Path(**file**).resolve().parent.parent / "libs"

## Before any change

- State which US-XXX user story this belongs to (@docs/specification/user-stories.md)
- State which test case validates this (@docs/specification/test-cases.md)
- Confirm no regression tests break (@docs/specification/test-cases.md section 9)

## Never without explicit approval

- Modify docs/
- Delete files
- Change core/ function signatures
- Add dependencies outside libs/
- Call sys.exit() outside cli/main.py

